(7784019, 1295395, 19959, '<td valign="top">
<table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by glad2badad:</b></div><hr/><i> Oh, I want to like this one so much.  Love the concept, just would have been stronger (IMO) with the DOF included down thru the camera and displayed photos.  Maybe the use of focus stacking would help here, especially in a static setting such as this?  Good luck. </i></td></tr></table>
<br/>
<br/>Thanks for the comment. I was kicking myself a little when you posted this during voting. I agree with you. I took a fair few different versions of the ''scene'' and this plain white was a last minute shot as I went to put everything away. In the end it felt clean enough to use but 100% I should have re-shot with better lighting (This was window light) and front to back focus (also improve the background (This was placed on top of the cats litterbox so sub-optimal for a product shoot :) )</td>', 'Originally posted by glad2badad: Oh, I want to like this one so much.  Love the concept, just would have been stronger (IMO) with the DOF included down thru the camera and displayed photos.  Maybe the use of focus stacking would help here, especially in a static setting such as this?  Good luck. 

Thanks for the comment. I was kicking myself a little when you posted this during voting. I agree with you. I took a fair few different versions of the ''scene'' and this plain white was a last minute shot as I went to put everything away. In the end it felt clean enough to use but 100% I should have re-shot with better lighting (This was window light) and front to back focus (also improve the background (This was placed on top of the cats litterbox so sub-optimal for a product shoot :) )', '2025-07-07 05:18:54.000000', NULL, 0),
